.SHORT TERM...
Issued at 1225 PM PST Sun Nov 15 2026
(This evening through Monday night)

Light to occasionally moderate rain continues over the North Bay
as the cold front moves through the region. More steady rain is
forecast to move into the Bay Area around 1 PM, the Santa Cruz
Mountains and the South Bay around 5 PM, and then the north
Central Coast beginning between 7 PM and 9 PM and beyond into
Monday morning. In wake of the frontal passage, post-frontal rain
showers are forecast to persist through Monday afternoon if not
the rest of the evening. Rainfall from this even will largely be
beneficial, yet cannot rule out minor nuisance flooding in low-
lying and poor drainage areas.

Southerly winds are increasing ahead of this front, yet are
forecast to be weaker than Friday`s system. Thus, expecting gusts
of 25 to 35 mph along the coast and through the favored gaps and
passes. Meanwhile, gusts up to 45 are forecast in the higher
terrain of the Bay Area. Winds have already becoming northwesterly
in areas of Marin and Sonoma county in wake of the frontal
passage.

A mix of sun and clouds are in the forecast for Monday afternoon,
yet isolated to scattered rain showers will still likely persist
over much of the region into Monday night.

