.MARINE...
(Today through Friday)
Issued at 849 AM PST Sun Nov 15 2026

Another cold front will move through the coastal waters bringing
unsettled weather with scattered light rain showers. Northwesterly
moderate to fresh winds develop behind the front this evening.
Very hazardous marine conditions and high northwest seas persist
through early Tuesday morning, with significant wave heights
between 15 to 20 feet. Seas subside slightly on Tuesday before
building again by Wednesday. This coincides with when a strong low
pressure system moves into the coastal waters resulting in
widespread rain, near gale to gale force winds, and potential for
thunderstorms.

