.BEACHES...
Issued at 1230 AM PST Sun Nov 15 2026

A High Surf Advisory is in effect now through Tuesday morning.
Long period swells 12 to 16 feet high at 14 to 16 seconds are
still coming through the coastal waters. Through the Advisory
period, breaking waves of 20-25 feet are expected with occasional
sets of 25-35 feet likely at favored breakpoints, including
Mavericks Beach. These waves are less energetic than the ones we
saw on Saturday, which ended up flooding portions of Pacifica and
damaging Capitola Pier, but remain hazardous to potential
swimmers, could still knock unaware people into the water, and
continue to feed an increased risk of rip currents. The risk of
drowning remains high. Do not go in the water, avoid climbing on
the rocks or leaning over seawalls, and never turn your back on
the ocean.

